WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.725
Here's the checklist, seven
questions an agency asks

2
00:00:03.725 --> 00:00:07.400
of each BIND server it adds
in AWS, as design guidance.

3
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:12.900
First establish whether they're EC2
instances or VMware guests on AWS.

4
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:18.925
One, role: a forwarder, resolver or
secondary aligns; a primary doesn't.

5
00:00:18.925 --> 00:00:24.575
Two, source of truth: no zones, or
zones transferred from the DDI platform.

6
00:00:24.575 --> 00:00:30.150
Three, why BIND: a stated need from the
criteria, or a bridge with an end date.

7
00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.299
Four, configuration: rendered,

8
00:00:32.299 --> 00:00:36.425
reviewed and applied by
automation, not edited on the host.

9
00:00:36.425 --> 00:00:39.889
Five, placement: the
hub VPC of each Region,

10
00:00:39.889 --> 00:00:43.150
at least two servers, rules shared once.

11
00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:48.232
Six, shared policy: logs in the
SIEM with the M-26-14 retention,

12
00:00:48.232 --> 00:00:53.950
the same policy-zone feed, and
Protective DNS as the only upstream.

13
00:00:53.950 --> 00:01:00.112
Seven: a supported branch, a stated
baseline, a CMDB record and a named owner.

14
00:01:00.112 --> 00:01:02.949
Rows two and four are the serious signals.

15
00:01:02.949 --> 00:01:06.770
Row three alone means the
servers may not be needed at all.
